=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: mswitch0
diagnosis_text:
**Affected component:** OSPF configuration on mswitch0 — the multilayer switch acting as the Layer-3 gateway for all Campus-1 VLANs (VLAN 10/20/30, prefixes 172.16.10.0/24, 172.16.20.0/24, 172.16.30.0/24).

**Mechanism:** mswitch0 has FRR installed and its daemon sockets are live (`vtysh=ok`), but its `running-config` is completely empty — no `router ospf` block, no `network` statements, no redistribution. As a result, mswitch0 never sends OSPF Hello packets on its uplink (`br0`, 10.2.2.2/24) toward router16's bond0 (10.2.2.1/24). That link therefore has zero adjacencies (`adj=0`), and the three Campus-1 subnets are never originated as Type-1/2 LSAs into the OSPF domain. Every router in the topology — including router11, router17, and sshswitch — has exactly the same 15 backbone routes and zero 172.16.x.x routes. When Campus-2 hosts (10.5.0.x, 10.6.0.x) attempt to reach Campus-1 IPs, their gateway (sshswitch, 10.5.0.254 / 10.6.0.254) has no matching route and returns ICMP "Destination Net Unreachable".

**Localization:** mswitch0, all interfaces (vlan10, vlan20, vlan30, br0). The adjacency that should exist on the mswitch0–router16 segment (10.2.2.0/24) is completely absent.

**Root cause:** mswitch0's OSPF configuration is entirely missing — an empty FRR config means it participates in no routing protocol and never advertises the Campus-1 prefixes into the OSPF domain.

**Why router11 is innocent:** router11 has full adjacencies and 15 correct OSPF routes; it simply never received any 172.16.x.x LSA because mswitch0 never sent one. Restarting router11 would have no effect.

**Fix:** Add an `router ospf` block to mswitch0's FRR configuration with `network 172.16.10.0/24 area 0.0.0.0`, `network 172.16.20.0/24 area 0.0.0.0`, `network 172.16.30.0/24 area 0.0.0.0`, and `network 10.2.2.0/24 area 0.0.0.0` so that the adjacency with router16 forms and Campus-1 prefixes propagate through the OSPF domain.
=== END ===